From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Menno <menno@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netlink: keep completion callback across transaction removal

The transaction hash table owns and frees each Transaction.  The receive path
removed a completed transaction and then called tr->completion_fn through the
freed object.  Whether that worked depended on the slice allocator retaining
the old contents.

On Myron this crashed ModemManager immediately after qmapmux0.0 was created:
the callback address had become 0x30 by the time transaction_complete() tried
to call it.  Copy the function pointer before removal, as the function already
does for the task and sequence id.
---
 src/mm-netlink.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mm-netlink.c b/src/mm-netlink.c
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/src/mm-netlink.c
+++ b/src/mm-netlink.c
@@ -229,9 +229,11 @@ transaction_complete (Transaction     *tr,
 {
     GTask *task;
+    MsgFunc completion_fn;
     guint32 sequence_id;
 
     task = g_steal_pointer (&tr->completion_task);
     sequence_id = tr->sequence_id;
+    completion_fn = tr->completion_fn;
 
     g_hash_table_remove (tr->self->transactions,
                          GUINT_TO_POINTER (tr->sequence_id));
@@ -240,7 +242,7 @@ transaction_complete (Transaction     *tr,
     if (!saved_errno) {
         GError *error = NULL;
 
-        if (!tr->completion_fn (task, hdr, &error))
+        if (!completion_fn (task, hdr, &error))
             g_task_return_error (task, error);
     } else {
         g_task_return_new_error (task, G_IO_ERROR, g_io_error_from_errno (saved_errno),
-- 
